package design

import . "github.com/goadesign/surla/story/dsl"

// The [[.Name]]'s Story says, in Surla's Story language, who uses the [[.Name]]
// and which paths their requests take. Surla evaluates it when the guide calls
// refresh_story, and keeps it with a change when the guide proposes or revises
// that change with the refresh's op_id (story_refresh_op_id). Every finished
// flow (one with a start, an outcome and no open question) is a test each
// build of a change requires: flow prices-cookie becomes the scenario
// prices_cookie of the evaluation suite in eval/, which the method PricesCookie
// of package eval/acceptance runs.
//
// To describe new behavior, the guide adds a flow here, calls refresh_story,
// and passes its op_id when it proposes or revises the change. A flow's key
// must not repeat a scenario the suite in eval/ already declares by hand:
// prices-tea would collide with prices_tea. The command
// go doc github.com/goadesign/surla/story/dsl lists the language.
var _ = Story("Prices", func() {
	Description("Customers ask the [[.Name]] what an item costs.")
	Actor("customer", "Customer")
	Flow("prices-cookie", "Price a cookie", func() {
		StartsWith("ask-cookie-price", "customer", "The customer asks how much a cookie is")
		Outcome("cookie-priced", "customer", "The helper answers that a cookie costs $1.25")
	})
})
